# Branching, Checkpoints, Backup, and Rollback

## Goal

Roleplay is exploratory. The app must support story branching and safe rollback without destroying continuity.

## Required features

### Checkpoints

- Save current story state
- Name the checkpoint
- Include world state, cast, and memory
- Include summary and sequence version

### Branching

- Branch from any turn or checkpoint
- Keep main branch and alternative branch separate
- Preserve raw turns and derived state for the branch
- Allow comparison of branch summaries

### Restore

- Restore a checkpoint or prior branch
- Restore the conversation cast and memory state together
- Alert the user that later story content will be invalidated

### Merge

- Only merge if the two branches are structurally compatible
- Show a preview of conflicts
- Leave both versions intact unless the user confirms

## Backup requirements

Include:

- character cards
- lorebooks
- conversations
- turn log
- cast state
- memories
- summary versions
- world state
- settings without secrets

## Migration requirement

Every backup and saved data file must carry a schema version.

## Final rule

No destructive action should occur without a preview and a confirm action.

---

This is non-negotiable for real roleplay use.
